 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Local network access
+
+Responses explicitly allow this application's origin to request local network and
+loopback access through `Permissions-Policy`. The browser still requires the
+user's permission; this header does not grant access automatically or delegate it
+to cross-origin frames.
+
+Serve the deployed application over HTTPS. Local services must allow the app's
+origin through standard CORS headers when the app reads cross-origin responses.
+For HTTP endpoints, client requests should set `targetAddressSpace: 'local'` for
+LAN devices or `targetAddressSpace: 'loopback'` for services on the user's machine.
+Initiate the first request from a user action, handle denied permissions and
+connection failures, and avoid querying the legacy `local-network-access`
+permission name.
+
